[{:adr/authoritative_for ["kototama.tender (kototama/src/kototama/tender.clj, :clj-only) is the first real execution layer for kototama.contract's HostCaps/RuntimeLimits/validate-import-surface -- pure data validation now has something that actually enforces it" "written fresh, not vendored from kotoba.wasm-exec, to avoid running kotoba's own incompatible kgraph/capability vocabulary alongside kototama's actor:host ABI (ADR-2607022700's semantic-authority-duplication rule)" "two distinct denial shapes: grant violation (:grant/missing) hard-throws (structural authority breach, not guest-recoverable); RuntimeLimits exhaustion signals in-band as -1 (same convention as write-bytes!'s overflow case, a guest can see it and back off) -- do not conflate the two" "ADR-2607022900's claim that quota/fuel/etc landed in aiueos-cljc-contract PRs #2-12 is verified FALSE (no such files/deps/commits exist in that repo) -- this ADR is the first with actually-running tender code" "verified against real Wasm binaries: wasm-tools-assembled WAT fixtures through the real Chicory Parser/Instance pipeline, not mocked -- 15 tests/31 assertions green" "addendum: aiueos.execute/aiueos.launcher (aiueos-cljc-contract's real main) already implements a similar-looking Chicory-hosted capability-gated execution path under aiueos's own manifest/broker vocabulary -- DECIDED to keep the two separate (different vocabularies for different problems: kototama.contract's cross-substrate actor:host ABI vs aiueos's OS-broker manifest/quota/topic/device vocabulary), not consolidate; aiueos calling kototama.tender/instantiate (translating a broker decision into a HostCaps value) remains an open follow-up, distinct from a code-level merge" "addendum 2: :max-memory-pages added to kototama.contract/RuntimeLimits (default 16 pages/1 MiB) and enforced in kototama.tender via Chicory's STABLE Instance.Builder/withMemoryLimits (not the :unsafe fuel-listener API tier), independent of which imports are granted -- 18 tests/35 assertions green" "addendum 3: verified kotoba wasm emit CANNOT call these 8 actor:host imports from real .kotoba source today -- the compiler resolves host-import calls against a CLOSED, hardcoded table (kotoba-core-contracts/resources/kotoba/runtime/capability_contract.edn's :host-imports/:host-import-order, merged with kotoba.runtime/cap-passing-imports), with no source-level FFI/import-declaration syntax; extending that table (in kotoba-core-contracts and kotoba, not kototama) is a prerequisite for a real .kotoba-source end-to-end test, tracked as a follow-up, not yet done" "addendum 4: :now/:log-append! renamed to :clock-monotonic/:log-write (kototama#21) to reuse names a concurrent session had already independently registered in kotoba-core-contracts' capability_contract.edn for aiueos's kernel-capability vocabulary (identical wire signatures) -- full detail and the matching wasm-webcomponent/kototama-web renames in ADR-2607062400's addendum" "addendum 5: addendum 3's E2E gap CLOSED -- kotoba-core-contracts#3 registered the 6 net-new actor:host imports (gen-keypair/sign/verify/sha256-hex/http-post/log-read, ids 219-224), kotoba#288 bumped its pin and added .kotoba demos proving no kotoba.runtime/op->kind changes were needed, kototama#23 checked in real kotoba-wasm-emit .wasm output (not WAT) as test fixtures and ran them through kototama.tender -- sha256-hex fixture computes sha256(\"\") correctly, gen-keypair fixture writes a real 32+32-byte seed/pubkey. 20 tests/38 assertions green in kototama, 131 tests/750 assertions green in kotoba" "addendum 6 (2026-07-07): the original addendum's premise was FALSE -- aiueos.execute/aiueos.launcher do NOT exist anywhere in this org (verified by reading the actual aiueos-cljc-contract checkout: src/aiueos/ has only data/validation .cljc files -- audit/broker/cli/contract/graph/manifest/policy/signing/surface/topic -- zero Chicory dependency, zero commits since 2026-07-02). The Chicory-based code the addendum was actually comparing against is kotoba.launcher/kotoba.wasm-exec in kotoba-lang/kotoba, a different repo with its own vocabulary. Same failure pattern ADR-2607022900 already caught once (fabricated aiueos implementation-status claim), repeated here -- recorded rather than silently corrected. The open follow-up (aiueos broker -> kototama.tender/instantiate adapter) is unaffected in substance and remains open." "addendum 7 (2026-07-07): the open follow-up CLOSED -- kototama.aiueos-adapter (kototama#24) calls aiueos.cli/command-result directly (a real io.github.kotoba-lang/aiueos dependency, in-process -- not the nbb-decide subprocess aiueos.decide also exposes for non-JVM hosts) and translates the real :grant/:deny decision into a kototama.contract/host-caps value, covering log-write/clock-monotonic/random-bytes (aiueos's default kernel capabilities). kototama.tender still never computes a grant itself. Verified end to end: a real aiueos :grant drives a real Chicory-hosted guest through kototama.tender to a real result; a real aiueos :deny (an unsigned component under a require-signed policy, aiueos's own ADR-0003 signature check) is what kototama.tender's pre-flight actually rejects -- no test-hardcoded HostCaps anywhere. 25 tests/50 assertions green" "addendum 8 (2026-07-07): a 9th import landed -- llm-infer (llm_infer, capability id 225), gated #{:network} and metered against a new :max-llm-infers limit like http-post, but built with an injectable llm-client ({:infer-fn}) instead of calling HttpClient inline -- default-llm-client resolves an API key from the same env-var chain cloud_itonami.runtime/model-config uses and calls the real Anthropic Messages API in production; tests inject a fake :infer-fn. Full story (cloud-itonami's isic-6511 underwriting governor compiled to a real .kotoba module and deployed without a JVM to a real murakumo fleet node, the parallel wasm-webcomponent/actor-host.js Node implementation, a .kotoba compiler bug found: and/or/when pass the safety gate but fail WASM codegen with unsupported-op) documented in ADR-2607072530, not duplicated here"], :adr/supersedes [], :adr/superseded_by [], :adr/topic "kototama-tender-chicory-execution-runtime", :adr/related ["adr-2607022400" "adr-2607022700" "adr-2607022900" "adr-2607061630" "adr-2607030900" "adr-2607062400" "adr-2607072530"], :adr/status "accepted", :adr/id "adr-2607062330-kototama-tender-chicory-execution-runtime", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-08", :adr/body "see 2607062330-kototama-tender-chicory-execution-runtime.md", :adr/deciders ["Jun Kawasaki"], :adr/artifacts "{:kototama \"kotoba-lang/kototama (kototama.tender namespace added, then :max-memory-pages, clock-monotonic/log-write rename, real .kotoba-compiled E2E fixtures, kototama.aiueos-adapter) — 25 tests/50 assertions green, JVM, real Wasm binaries (wasm-tools-assembled WAT AND real kotoba-wasm-emit output), real aiueos decisions\", :kotoba \"kotoba-lang/kotoba (kotoba-core-contracts pin bump + actor-host .kotoba demos, kotoba#288; real host-provider implementations, kotoba#289) — 144 tests/780 assertions green\", :kotoba-core-contracts \"kotoba-lang/kotoba-core-contracts (6 new actor:host host-imports registered, kotoba-core-contracts#3) — 7 tests/80 assertions green\", :aiueos \"kotoba-lang/aiueos (kototama.aiueos-adapter's real decision source, no changes made by this ADR -- aiueos.decide/aiueos.cli/aiueos.broker already existed) — 139 tests/399 assertions green\", :kotoba-lang \"kotoba-lang/kotoba-lang (effect-for-kind: 15 missing capability kinds registered, kotoba-lang/kotoba-lang#12) — 32 tests/227 assertions green\"}", :adr/date "2026-07-06", :db/id -1, :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607062330: kototama.tender — the Chicory/JVM execution runtime ADR-2607022900 decided on, landed"}]